<Page
  title="Cookie Policy"
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  updated="June 15, 2026"
  description="What cookies Em Dash Remover uses, why, and how to control them."
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how Em Dash Remover uses cookies and similar
    technologies. The core text-cleaning tool works without any cookies — it runs
    entirely in your browser. Cookies only come into play for optional analytics and
    advertising, and only with your consent.
  </p>

  <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored on your device by your browser. Similar
    technologies include local storage. We use local storage to remember your tool
    preferences and your consent choice; this never leaves your device.
  </p>

  <h2>Categories of cookies we use</h2>

  <h3>1. Strictly necessary (always on)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local storage</strong> — remembers your cleanup options, theme (light/dark), and your cookie-consent choice. Stored on your device only.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. Analytics (consent required)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Privacy-friendly analytics may set cookies to measure aggregate, anonymous traffic (page views, referrers). Loaded only after you accept.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. Advertising (consent required)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google AdSense and its partners may set cookies to serve and measure ads.
      For personalised ads in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, these are used only after
      consent via our Google-certified consent platform and Google Consent Mode.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Managing your choices</h2>
  <p>
    When you first visit, our banner lets you <strong>Accept</strong> or
    <strong>Decline</strong> analytics and advertising cookies. You can change your
    decision anytime using the
    <a href="#" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</a> link in the footer, or by
    clearing cookies and local storage in your browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also opt out of personalised advertising directly at
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>, and
    <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">optout.networkadvertising.org</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for full details on how data is
    handled, including the advertising disclosures required by Google.
  </p>
</Page>
